    "result_text": "The test passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented a stage filter that narrows the all-invoices list to a single status, following the app's additive conventions (no page or scaffolding edits). All invoices are already loaded client-side, so the feature is a pure front-end change keyed off the URL \u2014 no schema or server change was needed.\n\nNew/changed files:\n\n1. **`slots/defs/allInvoicesToolbar.ts`** (new) \u2014 declares a toolbar region above the cross-project invoices list (`invoices.all.toolbar`), since none existed yet (CLAUDE.md rule 3).\n\n2. **`features/invoices/status-filter.slot.tsx`** (new) \u2014 a self-contained `*.slot.tsx` control filling that region. It renders the `invoice-status-filter` `<select>` and owns the `invoiceStatus` URL search param (rule 4).\n\n3. **`features/invoices/queries.ts`** \u2014 added the `INVOICE_STATUS_PARAM` key and the `INVOICE_STATUSES` list (DRAFT/SENT/PAID) the filter offers.\n\n4. **`features/invoices/AllInvoicesTable.tsx`** \u2014 renders `<AllInvoicesToolbar.Slot />` and reads the same `invoiceStatus` key to drop rows at any other stage. The filter and list stay in step purely through the shared URL key \u2014 no callbacks or shared component state.\n\nThe `data-testid=\"invoice-status-filter\"` anchor and existing `invoice-row-*` anchors match the spec exactly, and `bin/e2e` passes (3 rows \u2192 2 SENT rows after selecting `SENT`).",
